new details have been released for  gearbox software's new game battle born  after a blog post on the 2k site I'm  Dave and welcome to your badass news  update in addition to the PC  requirements 2k and gearbox confirm that  battle bonds PC version supports  PlayStation 4 and Xbox one controllers  with support for the steam controller  coming after launch the PC version of  battle born will not support 4k or off  size displays at launch but the  developer is actively investigating both  to be added sometime further down the  road also featured in the blog post is  an overview of battle born game modes  and gameplay details among other things  it's confirmed that battle ball will  have a hardcore mode 4 story episodes  that give players unforgiving challenges  although there is no word yet on what  those are players will be rewarded for  their extra efforts as successful  players will earn extra loot and all new  unlockable content the blog post also  covers about abalones co-op support  there is local split-screen for ps4 and  Xbox one that supports 2 players per  system whilst also confirmed that  split-screen players can join any team  with the maximum number of players per  side being 5 be sure to read the full  blog post as it contains many more  details about battle bonds and numerous  roads and gameplay features Papelbon's  open beta begins on April 8 for ps4 and  April 13th for Xbox one and PC so are  you excited for battle born are you  badass enough to play let us know in the  comment section below or find me on  Twitter at irregular Dave and for your  gaming news station to GameSpot calm
 

